    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0183" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/612</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-04-04">April 4, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For the Secretary of State and the Under Secretary. I think it is important
                    enough for Davis to go to Berlin at once, to outweigh the Jewish problem.</p>
                <p>He should (&amp; we should) make it entirely clear to the public that he goes
                    there (1) because von Neurath will be away after Saturday &amp; (2) that he will
                    discuss only disarmament &amp; the economic conference dates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D. Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
